{"affected":[{"defaultStatus":"unknown","original_ranges":[{"status":"affected","version":"8.4.103"}],"product":"Ultralytics","vendor":"Ultralytics"}],"aliases":["CVE-2026-118619"],"assertions":[{"affected_indices":[0],"datePublic":"2026-10-28T16:31:36.742Z","descriptions":[{"lang":"en","value":"Ultralytics Google Drive Download Path Traversal Remote Code Execution Vulnerability. This vulnerability allows remote attackers to execute arbitrary code on affected installations of Ultralytics. User interaction is required to exploit this vulnerability in that the target must visit a malicious page or open a malicious file.\n\nThe specific flaw exists within the handling of downloads from Google Drive. The issue results from the lack of proper validation of a user-supplied path prior to using it in file operations. An attacker can leverage this vulnerability to execute arbitrary code in the context of the current process. Was ZDI-CAN-32376."}],"metrics":[{"cvssV3_0":{"baseScore":8.8,"baseSeverity":"HIGH","vectorString":"CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H","version":"3.0"},"format":"CVSS"}],"problemTypes":[{"descriptions":[{"cweId":"CWE-22","description":"CWE-22: Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory ('Path Traversal')","lang":"en","type":"CWE"}]}],"provider":{"dateUpdated":"2026-10-28T16:54:34.850Z","orgId":"99f1926a-a320-47d8-bbb5-42feb611262e","shortName":"zdi"},"role":"cna","title":"Ultralytics Google Drive Download Path Traversal Remote Code Execution Vulnerability"},{"affected_indices":[],"metrics":[{"other":{"content":{"id":"CVE-2026-118619","options":[{"Exploitation":"none"},{"Automatable":"no"},{"Technical Impact":"total"}],"role":"CISA Coordinator","timestamp":"2026-11-05T17:04:28.934669Z","version":"2.0.3"},"type":"ssvc"}}],"provider":{"dateUpdated":"2026-11-05T17:05:13.542Z","orgId":"134c704f-9b21-4f2e-91b3-4a467353bcc0","shortName":"CISA-ADP"},"role":"adp","title":"CISA ADP Vulnrichment"}],"assessment":{"authentication":null,"cl